# Everything in this repo that is a text file is consumed inside a Linux
# container (the Dockerfile's shell scripts, dockerdoom's autotools
# configure, every Makefile), so it must be checked out with LF endings
# regardless of the host's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with the common global
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites dockerdoom/trunk/configure's shebang to
# `#!/bin/sh\r`, and the build fails with the very unhelpful
# `./configure: not found` (exit 127) -- the file is right there, but
# Linux is looking for an interpreter literally named `/bin/sh\r`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.wad binary
*.png binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.part-* binary
